  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $\\mathrm{b}=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{t}}{\\mathrm{t}+1} d t$, then $\\int_{\\mathrm{a}-1}^{\\mathrm{a}} \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{-1}}{\\mathrm{t}-\\mathrm{a}-1}$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "sEzzg",
      "text": "be $^{a}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ptrbQ",
      "text": "be $^{-a}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ve5l9",
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{be}^{-\\mathrm{a}}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "3gHYm",
      "text": "$-\\mathrm{be}^{\\mathrm{a}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\int_{a-1}^{a} \\frac{e^{-t}}{t-a-1} d t$\r\n$=\\int_{\\mathrm{a}-1}^{\\mathrm{a}} \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{-(2 \\mathrm{a}-1-\\mathrm{t})}}{2 \\mathrm{a}-1-\\mathrm{t}-\\mathrm{a}-1} \\mathrm{dt}$\r\n$=\\int_{\\mathrm{a}-1}^{\\mathrm{a}} \\frac{\\mathrm{e}^{\\mathrm{t}-2 \\mathrm{a}+1}}{\\mathrm{a}-2-\\mathrm{t}} \\mathrm{dt}$\r\n$t-(a-1)=x \\quad \\Rightarrow d t=d x$\r\n$=\\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{e^{x} \\cdot e^{-a}}{-x-1} d x$\r\n$=-e^{-a} \\int_{0}^{1} \\frac{e^{x}}{x+1} d x=-b e^{-a}$",
    "image": null
  },
